cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md-195-
cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md-196-- **Hooks require feature flag:** The `codex_hooks` feature is `default_enabled: false` (stage: UnderDevelopment). It must be enabled via `--enable codex_hooks` CLI flag, or `features.codex_hooks = true` in `config.toml`, or `-c features.codex_hooks=true`. Without this, hooks.json is ignored entirely.
cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md-197-- **No SessionEnd hook:** Codex does not fire a hook when a session is completely terminated. The `Stop` hook fires at end-of-turn, not end-of-session. This is similar to some other agents — the framework handles this gracefully.
cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md-198-- **PreToolUse is shell-only:** Currently only fires for `Bash` tool (direct shell execution). MCP tools, stdin streaming, and other tool types are not yet hooked. PostToolUse is in review.
cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md-199-- **Transcript may be null:** In `--ephemeral` mode, `transcript_path` is null. The integration should handle this gracefully.
cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md-200-- **No subagent hooks:** No PreTask/PostTask equivalent for subagent spawning.
cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md:201:- **Hook response protocol differs from Claude Code:** Codex uses `systemMessage` (same field name) but also supports `hookSpecificOutput` with `additionalContext` for injecting context into the model. For Entire's purposes, `systemMessage` is sufficient.
